<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Bagerhat</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Khalifatabad</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Bagerhat is a town in south-western Bangladesh, in the Sundarbans region. In the 15th century the frontier <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/magnates">magnate</a> Khan Jahan Ali founded a settlement there, called Khalifatabad, with mosques, tombs, roads and water tanks. Its surviving brick monuments, led by the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/sixty-dome-mosque">Sixty Dome Mosque</a>, were inscribed as the Historic Mosque City of Bagerhat World Heritage Site in 1985.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/bagerhat.jpg" alt="Bagerhat" width="320" height="213" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Faisallutpat2 · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Bagerhat_Central_Shahid_Minar.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
